      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buford%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "European settlement in the Buford area began during the mid-eighteenth century with Scotch-Irish and German migrations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/buford_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Buford emerged as a small farming outpost in the post-Revolutionary War era within the rural Piedmont region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/buford_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A small church operated on the grounds of Buford from 1893 to 1902.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/buford_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Buford preserved its agricultural character through family-owned lands well into the twentieth century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
